# Sleeping Clanker API keys - TEMPLATE (2026-10-20, docs/SPEC_V047_PROVIDERS.md)
#
# Copy this file to %LOCALAPPDATA%\claud_autopilot\providers.env (OUTSIDE every repo) and fill in
# only the keys you have. THIS template is the only copy git sees, so keep it key-free.
#
#   .venv\Scripts\python -m sleeping_clanker providers             # what is set, what is missing
#   .venv\Scripts\python -m sleeping_clanker run --provider deepseek
#   .venv\Scripts\python -m sleeping_clanker run --provider codex --model gpt-5.1
#
# Where the file is looked for (first one that exists wins):
#   1. `run --env-file PATH` / `providers --env-file PATH`
#   2. %CLAUDE_AUTOPILOT_ENV_FILE%
#   3. <project data dir>\providers.env   - per project (`autopilot where` prints the folder)
#   4. %LOCALAPPDATA%\claud_autopilot\providers.env   - one file for every project
# (2026-10-21) A repo is NEVER searched: not the folder autopilot is started from and not this
# checkout. A `.env` here is ignored with one WARNING: a task that can write its repo could otherwise
# route the next run to any endpoint. Tools are denied Read/Edit/Write of .env, .env.* and
# providers.env, and shell-read/shell-dev items refuse to run while a provider key is in use.
#
# Syntax: KEY=VALUE, one per line. `#` starts a comment, quotes are optional, an `export ` prefix is
# allowed, and there is no ${substitution}. An empty value counts as "not set".
#
# Only the keys of the provider a run actually uses are put into the claude.exe child environment:
# a DeepSeek run never sees the OpenAI key. Every base URL and model below can be overridden here.
# Heads up: deny rules are not a sandbox; keep the key file out of every repo.

# ---- which provider a run uses when `run --provider NAME` is not given ----------------------------
# claude (default) | claude-api | deepseek | kimi | glm | qwen | codex | bedrock | custom
CLAUDE_AUTOPILOT_PROVIDER=claude

# ---- claude: Claude Code on the claude.ai subscription (no key) -----------------------------------
# Nothing to set: claude.exe uses its own `/login` session and the run is not billed per token.

# ---- claude-api: the same Claude models, paid from an Anthropic Console key ----------------------
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=
# CLAUDE_API_MODEL=claude-opus-5-5

# ---- deepseek ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
DEEPSEEK_API_KEY=
# DEEPSEEK_MODEL=deepseek-chat
# DEEPSEEK_BASE_URL=https://api.deepseek.com/anthropic

# ---- kimi (Moonshot) -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
MOONSHOT_API_KEY=
# KIMI_API_KEY=                      # the same key under the other accepted name
# KIMI_MODEL=kimi-k2-turbo-preview
# KIMI_BASE_URL=https://api.moonshot.ai/anthropic

# ---- glm (Z.ai) ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
ZAI_API_KEY=
# GLM_API_KEY=                       # the same key under the other accepted name
# GLM_MODEL=glm-4.6
# GLM_BASE_URL=https://api.z.ai/api/anthropic

# ---- qwen (Alibaba DashScope) --------------------------------------------------------------------
DASHSCOPE_API_KEY=
# QWEN_API_KEY=                      # the same key under the other accepted name
# QWEN_MODEL=qwen3-coder-plus
# QWEN_BASE_URL=https://dashscope-intl.aliyuncs.com/api/v2/apps/claude-code-proxy

# ---- codex: OpenAI / Codex models, through an Anthropic-compatible gateway -----------------------
# claude.exe speaks the Anthropic wire format only, and OpenAI's API does not. So this provider
# needs a translating gateway (e.g. a LiteLLM proxy running on this machine) and stays "not ready"
# until CODEX_BASE_URL points at one.
OPENAI_API_KEY=
# CODEX_API_KEY=                     # the same key under the other accepted name
CODEX_BASE_URL=
# CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5.1-codex

# ---- bedrock: Claude on AWS Bedrock --------------------------------------------------------------
# A bearer token, or the usual AWS access key pair. Bedrock model ids are region-specific, so
# BEDROCK_MODEL has no default.
AWS_BEARER_TOKEN_BEDROCK=
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# BEDROCK_MODEL=

# ---- custom: any other Anthropic-compatible endpoint (the escape hatch) --------------------------
# Use this for a gateway, a router (claude-code-router, LiteLLM) or a provider not listed above.
CUSTOM_API_KEY=
CUSTOM_BASE_URL=
CUSTOM_MODEL=

# The base URLs above come from each provider's documentation and were NOT probed from this machine
# (2026-10-20): if one of them moves, set <PROVIDER>_BASE_URL here instead of waiting for a release.
